# Apple UI screenshots (mandatory)

When a change **alters user-visible UI** on iPhone and/or Apple Watch, agents **must** refresh the matching screenshots before marking the work done (or before PR/merge).

## When this applies

Triggers (any of):

- New or changed SwiftUI screens, layout, copy, navigation, empty states, charts, controls
- Watch glance / Always On / workout UI changes
- Public README or docs that display those screenshots

Does **not** apply to: pure backend/protocol/.NET Bridge, HealthKit adapters with no UI delta, docs-only non-visual edits, test-only changes.

## Where files live

| Platform | Directory | Index |
| --- | --- | --- |
| watchOS | `docs/screenshots/watchos/` | `docs/screenshots/watchos/README.md` |
| iOS | `docs/screenshots/ios/` | `docs/screenshots/ios/README.md` |

Update the platform README table (filename, mode, launch args, simulator, date). If the root `README.md` embeds shots, refresh those embeds too.

## How to capture (simpulse-mac)

Prefer DEBUG launch arguments / mocks so HealthKit permission is not required (same pattern as Watch `--simpulse-preview-*`).

```sh
# Watch example
xcrun simctl io <watch-udid> screenshot docs/screenshots/watchos/<name>.png

# iPhone example
xcrun simctl io <iphone-udid> screenshot docs/screenshots/ios/<name>.png
```

Record UDID / device model / Xcode version in the platform README. Physical-device shots are optional extras, not a substitute when simulator shots exist.

## Definition of done gate

A UI-affecting Apple backlog item is **not** DONE until:

1. Screenshots for the changed surface(s) are updated (or newly added)
2. `docs/screenshots/<platform>/README.md` lists them
3. Handoff notes “screenshots updated” (or “NOT EXECUTED — no Mac” if capture was impossible — then leave CURRENT_STATE explicit)

Do not ship stale Watch/iPhone marketing or docs images after a visible UI change.
